1
00:00:00,145 --> 00:00:02,480
This is the Wall of ScrappyT.

2
00:00:02,938 --> 00:00:05,599
Its 41 Cents hold every one of the nineteen

3
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:07,200
traits in the Traits Atlas.

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,359
As of October 2026,

5
00:00:09,439 --> 00:00:12,119
no other Wall on cents.vision does.

6
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,240
Even the artist wallet,

7
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:16,039
with a thousand Cents, has no Iridescent Cent.

8
00:00:16,457 --> 00:00:19,000
Its signature Cent, number 7139,

9
00:00:19,039 --> 00:00:21,800
from 1967, carries two of them:

10
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,320
a full desert patina, and Ghost.

11
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:26,399
Ghost means a full or near-full

12
00:00:26,519 --> 00:00:29,013
patina sets Lincoln apart from the field.

13
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:30,600
Of the thirty-three Ghost Cents,

14
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:33,292
only thirteen carry a full desert patina.

15
00:00:33,439 --> 00:00:36,246
Here are the other seventeen, one Cent each.

16
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:40,807
Verdigris, green to teal: number 8550, significant.

17
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:43,119
Obsidian, dark brown to black:

18
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,767
number 8394, significant.

19
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:50,173
Red, scarlet to russet: number 9258, full.

20
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,039
Notable means clearly visible but local,

21
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,320
significant a major presence on the face,

22
00:00:55,359 --> 00:00:58,167
and full means the patina dominates the coin.

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,487
Gold, honey gold to pale amber: number 5856.

24
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:07,049
Orange, given only to clear standouts: number 9469.

25
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,439
Iridescent, a copper surface overlaid

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,319
with gold, violet and blue: number 7713.

27
00:01:13,359 --> 00:01:16,486
Only twenty Cents carry it, and this Wall holds two.

28
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,239
Corroded, oxidation that has

29
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:21,206
gone into the metal: number 366.

30
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:24,887
Lustrous, original mint shine: number 830.

31
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:27,359
Striated, parallel lines made by metal

32
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:30,326
flow during striking: number 1295.

33
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,040
Abraded, copper missing from gouges:

34
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,772
number 8136, heavily abraded.

35
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:40,093
Faceless, Lincoln's features lost: number 1965.

36
00:01:40,239 --> 00:01:42,000
Fingerprint, ridges clear enough

37
00:01:42,079 --> 00:01:44,412
to read at once: number 508.

38
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,186
White drips and streaks,

39
00:01:46,212 --> 00:01:49,766
pale runs across the patina: number 2654.

40
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,239
Contaminated, foreign matter added after

41
00:01:52,359 --> 00:01:54,359
minting: four of the twelve types,

42
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,560
special oddities, obscure adhesive,

43
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,566
speckles and alien secretion.

44
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,040
Assassin, one round mark on Lincoln's

45
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,959
head, neck or body: number 739.

46
00:02:04,159 --> 00:02:06,079
Vandalized, marks that show

47
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:10,319
deliberate human intent: number 7745.

48
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,360
Only twenty-six Cents carry it.

49
00:02:12,772 --> 00:02:15,759
And Wheat, struck 1958 or earlier,

50
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,360
with wheat ears on the back:

51
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:20,639
number 3824, from 1956,

52
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:22,240
the earliest year on the Wall.

53
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:24,560
Nineteen of nineteen.

54
00:02:24,706 --> 00:02:26,240
The Wall spans two wallets

55
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:29,360
and the years 1956 to 1982,

56
00:02:29,479 --> 00:02:30,879
which puts it in the Quarter Club,

57
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,199
for twenty-five to forty-nine Cents.

58
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:36,560
It completes six Sets, among them a Spectrum Set:

59
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:39,680
all four base patinas, plus gold and orange.

60
00:02:39,719 --> 00:02:42,400
As of October 2026, ScrappyT is one

61
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:45,039
of only fifteen collectors to hold one.

62
00:02:45,112 --> 00:02:47,039
The Wall carries Diamond Hands:

63
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,719
it has held its position for at least

64
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,039
a year, with little to no selling.

65
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,360
And it is a Mint Keeper: ScrappyT

66
00:02:53,479 --> 00:02:54,719
minted four of its Cents

67
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,120
and still holds them, never sold.

68
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,800
Find all of the Collector Walls

69
00:02:58,879 --> 00:03:01,360
